1. Attribution of third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Provenance depends on the third-party components listed below. No source code
from any of them has been copied into this repository; each is consumed as a
published package or as a network service through its public interface. Each
component is distributed by its own authors under its own licence terms, which
are NOT restated here - a paraphrased licence is a wrong licence. Consult the
LICENSE file shipped inside each distribution. The package manifests resolve to
exact, pinned artifacts at build time: requirements-runtime.txt and
pyproject.toml for Python, apps/web/package.json and its lockfile for the web
application.

Versions are deliberately not pinned in this file. The manifests are the single
place a version is recorded, and a version duplicated here would drift from them.

This list was rewritten on 2026-08-31 to match what the build actually installs.
Until then it described the AWS build this project began as - LangGraph, boto3,
the AWS CDK, Bedrock, S3, SES, EventBridge, Textract and Bedrock AgentCore - and
named no Google component at all, a week after the pivot recorded in PIVOT.md
moved the models to Gemini and the hosting to Cloud Run. An attribution file
that credits software the product does not use, and omits the software it does,
is wrong in the direction that matters most: it fails to credit. The AWS entries
that remain below are here because that code is still committed in this
repository, and each one says what it is.

